{%- comment -%}
  Product aggregateRating JSON-LD — sourced from the Judge.me review metafield, the same
  source this theme's own snippets/reviews-star-rating.liquid already reads from
  (product.metafields.judgeme.review_widget_data). Emitted ONLY when a product has at least
  one real review — Google requires reviewCount > 0, and an empty/fabricated rating is worse
  than none.
  DATA CHECK 2026-08-07 (verified via debug render, then removed): sampled 8 live products
  spanning publish dates back to Dec 2024 — all show 0 accumulated Judge.me reviews,
  metafield last synced 2026-08-06 (identical timestamp across every product — a full fresh
  sync, not gradual accumulation). This contradicts the Product SEO Audit (2026-08-06)'s
  assumption that reviews already existed — flagged as an open discrepancy, not silently
  resolved. The "52+ reviews" homepage copy is Google Business Profile reviews (a different
  entity, already schema'd on the homepage JewelryStore block), not Shopify product reviews.
  Net effect: this fix currently renders for 0 live products but is correctly wired for when
  real reviews land — no manual follow-up needed once Judge.me accumulates reviews.
  Added 2026-08-07.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if template contains 'product' -%}
  {%- assign review_data = product.metafields.judgeme.review_widget_data.value -%}
  {%- if review_data.number_of_reviews > 0 -%}
  <script type="application/ld+json">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org/",
    "@type": "Product",
    "name": {{ product.title | json }},
    "sku": {{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.sku | json }},
    "aggregateRating": {
      "@type": "AggregateRating",
      "ratingValue": {{ review_data.average_rating | json }},
      "reviewCount": {{ review_data.number_of_reviews | json }}
    }
  }
  </script>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
